From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:42:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Onefile: Avoid decompression and checksums for unchanged
 cached mode unpacking

In cached mode, every start decompressed the whole payload and computed
the CRC32 of every unpacked file, costing time proportional to the
payload size even when nothing changed.

Now a completed unpacking writes a manifest file, tied to the payload by
a build time hash and recording size, mtime, and inode of every unpacked
file. When all of these match, the next start skips decompression and
checksumming entirely and only stats the files. Any mismatch falls back
to the previous full verification path, which repairs the files and
writes a new manifest. The manifest is removed before unpacking and
committed via rename, so an interrupted unpacking is never trusted.

For a 40MB payload on macOS, warm start goes from 80.8ms to 18.9ms,
with standalone at 17.2ms.

See #4028
---
 nuitka/build/static_src/OnefileBootstrap.c | 550 +++++++++++++++++----
 nuitka/freezer/Onefile.py                  |  16 +-
 2 files changed, 464 insertions(+), 102 deletions(-)

